Z||000007||AusFiero||06-08-2001||10:10 PM||||To answer some questions.<P>The sony sub should really have 0.5 cubic feet of air. Mine has less and does sounds great once I adjusted my bass levels etc on my system but there is 4 cubic feet options available 0.35 0.4 0.51 and 0.6. <P>The different sizes come from making it 1" deeper and/or removing the cd holder on top of the console. Have also discovered you can delete the cd holder and use a tube sub facing upwards. Not sure on which brands would work for that option though.<P>Cosole production is full swing now and I can ship within 24 hours of receiving payment, excluding heaps of orders all arriving on the 1 day of course. Then there may be up to a 4 day shipping delay as I am only human and work 16 hours a day now.<P>I am trying to make stocks though to keep on the shelf.<P>All details on pricing and sizes etc can be found in the original thread on the mall listed at the top of this post.<P>It arrives as a precut, predrilled ready to assemble kit in bare MDF board. All screws are also supplied as is assembly instructions. Am actually refining the instructions now to include full photo assembly instruction to make life easier for people. <P>All you need to buy for basic assembly is some wood glue as I can't ship that due to customs etc. <P>Upholstering the console is easy with the instructions supplied. You will need some thin foam, covering of your choice, some spray on contact cement and a staple gun. A decent staple gun is cheap at any hardware store. You will also need a tube of silicon sealant to mount your trim plates. I found this best as it builds a vibration proof layer between the plate and console and eliminates any chance of vibration or sound distortion. I had to try a few methods to get that to work out originally.<P>The carbon fibre is a quality stick on I used on mine but if you want carbon fibre I can supply you with enough of the same I used, to do your own console, gearshift plate, radio plate and gauge panel(including the GT Centre gauges) for an extra $25. It is really easy to apply and looks the part if you have looked at my other interior pics around. Not sure what the stick on is worth in the states so check on that if you like as you may find it cheaper. Just watch the quality though for your own sake.<P>I could also supply a complete upholstery kit, excluding the afor mentioned trim plates and staples) for about $20, will have to work that out though first to be sure on price. It may be cheaper. Could supply it in a basic grey or beige but you would have to dye it or spray it to match your interior like I did.<P>Need any other info? Just ask and I will be happy to oblige.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
